.TH FERRIS-BROWSER 1 "2026" "ferris-browser 1.0.0" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
ferris-browser \- a from-scratch browser engine written in Rust
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ferris-browser
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGUMENTS\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ferris-browser
implements the whole browser pipeline itself: HTTP(S) fetching, HTML parsing
into a DOM, a CSS cascade, layout, painting, and a native window (Wayland or
X11) with browser furniture (tab strip, omnibox).  It can also run page
JavaScript when built with the
.I js
Cargo feature (Boa engine).
.PP
With no arguments a short command summary is printed.
.PP
With no arguments (or with a bare URL) the native browser window is opened —
the start page, or the given URL.  This is what the desktop entry launches.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR serve " [\-\-port N]"
Run the browser UI over HTTP on the given port (default 8080): point any
browser at it to use the engine headlessly.
.TP
.BR window " URL [\-\-width N] [\-\-height H]"
Open the native window and browse the given URL.  Requires a display server
(WAYLAND_DISPLAY or DISPLAY).
.TP
.BR shot " URL [\-\-width N] [\-\-height H] [\-o FILE]"
Render the page headlessly and write a PNG (default out.png).
.TP
.BR info " URL"
Print parse/layout statistics for the page.
.TP
.BR shelltest " URL [more URLs] [\-\-width N] [\-o FILE]"
Headless check that the window's interactive path renders the given pages.
.TP
.BR jscorpus " [URLs...]"
Run the bundled JavaScript compatibility corpus (requires the
.I js
feature); exits non-zero on any failing entry.
.TP
.BR version ", " help
Print the version / the command summary.
.SH BUILD FEATURES
.TP
.I js
Page JavaScript via the Boa engine (no ICU).
.TP
.I js-date
Adds Date/Temporal support on top of
.IR js .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.I WAYLAND_DISPLAY ", " DISPLAY
Select the display server for
.BR window .
Headless commands (serve, shot, info, shelltest, jscorpus, version) work
without either.
.SH FILES
The DejaVu typefaces and the application icon are embedded in the binary;
their licences ship in /usr/share/licenses/ferris-browser/.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; non-zero on failure (including any failing
.B jscorpus
entry).
